#2979=IFCDOORTYPE('3uX93FFCfNtgC6mQmf9gyC',$,'D1','Patio door, 60 x 80 in. Safety glazing: IBC 2018 2406.4.1 calls for it here.',$,(#2988,#2980,#2984),$,$,$,.DOOR.,.NOTDEFINED.,$,$);
#2980=IFCPROPERTYSET('1aP1UIm6fS3AKG45HBb6TV',$,'Pset_DoorCommon',$,(#2981,#2982,#2983));
#2981=IFCPROPERTYSINGLEVALUE('Reference',$,IFCIDENTIFIER('D1'),$);
#2982=IFCPROPERTYSINGLEVALUE('IsExternal',$,IFCBOOLEAN(.T.),$);
#2983=IFCPROPERTYSINGLEVALUE('ThermalTransmittance','params systems.addendum_4.window_u_max (high): 0.22 Btu/h ft2 F, the most whole-unit U-factor of the windows and patio doors (NFRC 100); ENERGY STAR''s criteria table, v7 (October 2023, https://www.energystar.gov/sites/default/files/asset/document/ES_Windows_Table_Oct2023.pdf), as a research agent read it (2026-11-21): Northern zone, prescriptive, ''U-Factor <= 0.22'', ''SHGC >= 0.17''; every Pennsylvania ZIP code starting 15 or 16 is Northern (ENERGY STAR''s ''V7 ES Zones by Zip Code''). The code asks 0.30 (PA 2021 IECC zone 5). Sold, NFRC-certified: Pella 250 Series vinyl casement, SunDefense+ Low-E, argon, foam-insulated frame, PEL-A-287-00292-00001, U 0.22, SHGC 0.18; its fixed unit PEL-A-289-00258-00001, U 0.22, SHGC 0.22 (Pella 2026 Architectural Design Manual); its Standard sliding patio door, 1 in. triple-pane SunDefense Low-E, 4/4/4 mm, argon, WDI-A-33-02762-00001, U 0.19, SHGC 0.23 (Pella 2025 ADM, 250-SPD, read by me)',IFCTHERMALTRANSMITTANCEMEASURE(1.2492178600000001),$);
#2984=IFCPROPERTYSET('23_0K5_inRee$gmD4W0hUA',$,'Pset_DoorWindowGlazingType',$,(#2985,#2990));
#2985=IFCPROPERTYSINGLEVALUE('SolarHeatGainTransmittance','params systems.addendum_4.shgc_max (high): 0.25 the most solar heat gain coefficient of the windows and patio doors (NFRC 200, the whole unit); the design (pass 3g step 3c): at the placeholder 0.35 no 1-ton unit covers a flat''s cooling (Fujitsu''s 12k gives 2.77 kW sensible on the ground floor''s line set against 3.37 kW); at 0.25 the worst flat needs 2.62 kW and the 12k serves. The winter sun it gives up is heat the data center supplies. Such units are sold, NFRC-certified (makers'' tables, a research agent''s reading and mine, 2026-11-21): Pella 250 Series vinyl casement, 3/4 in. SunDefense Low-E, argon, PEL-A-287-00157-00001, U 0.26, SHGC 0.18; its fixed unit PEL-A-289-00122-00001, U 0.26, SHGC 0.22 (Pella 2026 Architectural Design Manual); its Standard sliding patio door, 3/4 in. SunDefense Low-E, 5 mm glass, argon, WDI-A-33-02494-00001, U 0.27, SHGC 0.21 (Pella 2025 ADM, 250-SPD); Pella Impervia fiberglass casement PEL-N-277-00243-00001, U 0.28, SHGC 0.20. Not ENERGY STAR v7 in its Northern zone (all of western Pennsylvania), which asks U at most 0.22 with SHGC at least 0.17',IFCNORMALISEDRATIOMEASURE(0.25),$);
