#3002=IFCPROPERTYSINGLEVALUE('FireRating','params bidset.code.exit_stair.door_rating_h (high): 1 hours, the fire protection rating of a door assembly (door, frame, hardware) in the stair''s enclosure, such as a flat''s entry door; labelled D-H-60, self-closing and latching; IBC 2018 chapter 7, on UpCodes (Pennsylvania Building Code 2018), the page as Jon saved it 2026-11-20: Table 716.1(2) Opening fire protection assemblies, ratings and markings, row ''Fire barriers having a required fire-resistance rating of 1 hour: Enclosures for shafts, exit access stairways, exit access ramps, interior exit stairways and interior exit ramps; and exit passageway walls'': wall 1 h, minimum fire door assembly rating 1 h, vision panel 100 sq. in. (D-H-60 up to 100 sq. in., D-H-T-W-60 above), sidelights and transoms: fire protection not permitted, fire resistance 1 h (W-60). 716.2.6.1 ''Fire doors shall be latching and self- or automatic-closing''. 716.2.2.3''s 450 F temperature-rise limit at 30 minutes doesn''t apply in a building sprinklered throughout (903.3.1.1 or 903.3.1.2), which the single exit needs anyway. 716.1: installed per NFPA 80',IFCLABEL('1 h'),$);
